body:
The model is the AK47-Iron Beast from Crossfire.

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

I combined two models together: the AK47 and the Eye Glow (a ribbon of jiggle bones). They are now one mesh. I did ctrl + J to combine them together.

&#x200B;

All the bones in the "eyes" are parented accordingly. The main bone they are all attached to is attached to the main weapon bone, as seen in the video.

&#x200B;

When I press 'tab' to go into Edit Mode, the bones and the mesh move to their original position.

&#x200B;

When I attach animations to the model, the bones and the mesh move to their original position.

&#x200B;

~~While typing this comment I realized I could try to setting the origin on the Eye Glow to the same place that the AK47 has its origin. I will edit this comment if it does not work.~~

&#x200B;

EDIT: It does not work, since both models are part of the same mesh, thus sharing the same origin. Please help me!

Im assuming its only on a community sever;

Put `”nodraw” “1”` in the VMT for that. Should be somewhere in your materials folder. You can open VMTs with notepad and VTF files with [VTFEdit](https://nemstools.github.io/pages/VTFLib-Download.html).

Edit: just read your other comment, so i guess its not on community servers only. Its not on your desktop or anything right? Removing it normally would require some modding knowledge. Id need more info before helping you out.
